# Todo 13 — Windows tray Restart/Exit wiring

Contract under test: Todo 13 requires the `wifimic-client` tray to keep the hidden-by-default Windows client behavior, create the embedded tray resource and menu, pump Win32 messages on the tray-creation thread, call `ControlPlane::restart()` directly for Restart without an implicit Stop, and call `ControlPlane::stop()` before terminating only the current process run for Exit. The Scheduled Task remains responsible for the next logon.

## Implementation

- Added `apps/wifimic_client/src/tray.rs` with canonical tooltip `wifimic-client`, `Restart`/`Exit` IDs, typed tray errors, same-thread `TrayRuntime`, native `MenuEvent::receiver()` mapping, and the non-blocking Win32 message pump.
- Added the injected `TrayControl`/`MenuEvent` seam and `tray_tests.rs`; Restart forwards exactly once and returns the fresh ID supplied by the control seam. Exit calls Stop, then marks shutdown, and `render_if_running` suppresses all later rendering.
- Added Windows-only `tray-icon`, `windows`, and `embed-resource` wiring; `assets/tray-icon.rc` uses canonical resource ordinal `1 ICON "tray-icon.ico"` and the copied icon has ICO signature `00000100`, 115474 bytes.
- Added the Windows subsystem attribute so no console window is introduced for the background tray client.

